      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1342294252,
      "text": "Lycium barbarum is a shrub native to China, with present-day range across Asia and southeast Europe. It is one of two species of boxthorn in the family Solanaceae from which the goji berry or wolfberry is harvested, the other being Lycium chinense."
    }
